.TH xargs 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
xargs \- build command lines from standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xargs
[\fB\-n\fI max\fR] [\fB\-s\fI chars\fR] [\fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xargs
reads words from standard input and runs
.I command
with them appended to any
.I arguments
already given, repeating until the input runs out.  With no
.IR command ,
it runs
.BR /bin/echo .
.PP
Words are separated by whitespace; quoting is not understood, so a file
name containing a space arrives as two arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " max"
Pass at most
.I max
words to each invocation.  The default is 20.
.TP
.BI \-s " chars"
Accepted and remembered, but not yet used to limit anything.
.SH LIMITS
Up to 20 words per command line and 10 fixed arguments before them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# ls *.bas | xargs wc -l
# find / -name core | xargs rm
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR sh (1)
